Reading the budget:
  efficiency = extractable / work_in — the sorted state's free energy comes
  from the heat jet's external work, so the second law is bounded by this
  ratio (<< 1 here), not by the Landauer column.
  bits_need = extractable work priced in Landauer bits at 300 K — the memory
  traffic a demon would need to write per trial for its erasure bill to match
  the work it gains. bits_used = decision flips + feedback bits actually
  metered. bits_used << bits_need means this demon barely memorizes: its
  erasure cost is negligible and its sorting is jet-subsidized, not
  information-driven. That is the honest thermodynamic budget, not a
  second-law violation.
